    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0515" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg455"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 118.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 23, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A further auction with the sum of forty
                    thousand dollars, for the purchase of bonds of the English and Spanish
                    convention debts by this government, was held on the 21st instant.</p>
                <p>I transmit herewith, for the information of the department, translation of the
                    order directing such auction to be held, and of the official report of the
                    result of the same.</p>
                <p>It has been a subject of remark that the only person appearing as a vendor at
                    this sale, for both of these debts, is an individual who is reported to be a
                    confidential agent of government officials.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. L. PLUMB.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




                <xi:include href="d290-a1.xml" xpointer="d290-a1"/>
